@startuml composite-emission
title US-06: Composite Emission - Atomic Insert + Active Alert Supersession

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts" as TSDB
database "Redis\nalert-events" as AlertEvents
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish deterministic COMPOSITE\n{ alert_id, pair_key, dark_since_ms,\n supersedes_alert_ids, ... }
Kafka -> API : consume COMPOSITE

API -> TSDB : BEGIN
API -> TSDB : INSERT COMPOSITE status=NEW\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING
API -> TSDB : UPDATE referenced individual alert(s)\nSET status='SUPERSEDED', superseded_by=$composite_id\nWHERE alert_id IN (...)\nAND status IN ('NEW','ACKNOWLEDGED')
API -> TSDB : COMMIT

note over TSDB
  Insert occurs before setting the FK reference.
  Both operations are in one transaction.
  Only active alerts are superseded.
  RESOLVED and already-SUPERSEDED rows are terminal.
  Replay converges on the same composite alert_id.
end note

API -> AlertEvents : PUBLISH ALERT_CREATED for COMPOSITE
API -> AlertEvents : PUBLISH ALERT_SUPERSEDED\nfor each row actually transitioned

note over API, AlertEvents
  Pub/sub/WebSocket delivery may repeat under replay.
  Durable TimescaleDB state is authoritative.
end note

AlertEvents --> Dashboard : lifecycle events via API WebSocket fan-out
Dashboard -> Dashboard : converge by alert_id + current status

@enduml
